cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the released tables, please cite the accompanying manuscript."
title: "DART-Det: density-adaptive rank-truncation diagnosis and training-free budget repair for NMS-free detection"
abstract: >-
  Diagnosis-and-repair code for the fixed decode budget of end-to-end, NMS-free
  detectors. Treats the fixed top-K stage as a rate-constrained ranked-selection
  channel, names the loss Rank-Truncation Information Loss (RTIL), decomposes the
  density-stratified recall drop into a recoverable budget-truncation term, an
  shared-difficulty term that the one-to-many reference path also fails to
  recover at the cached rank depth, and a small residual between the two
  evaluated decode paths, and
  repairs the recoverable term at inference with DABA (Density-Adaptive Budget
  Allocation), a training-free density-to-budget rule.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/7staranr/DART-Det"
keywords:
  - object detection
  - NMS-free detection
  - fixed-budget set prediction
  - rank truncation
  - dense object detection
  - density-adaptive inference
